<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Someshvara II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1068">1068</a>–<a href="/years/1076">1076</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Someshvara II was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a> from 1068 to 1076, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/someshvara-i">Someshvara I</a>. His reign was troubled by conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> and by the rivalry of his younger brother Vikramaditya, who held the southern provinces from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banavasi">Banavasi</a> and allied with the Chola king Virarajendra. In 1076 Vikramaditya deposed him and became king as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-vi">Vikramaditya VI</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/someshvara-ii.jpg" alt="Someshvara II" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jugaari cross · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Kannada_inscription_dated_Shaka_990_(c.1068_AD)_of_Kalyani_(Western)_Chalukya_King_Bhuvanaikamalla_Someshvara_II.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
